{"id":"chatcmpl-0bb55764-e0d4-45b1-8742-af893039c388","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248575,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-model consensus strategy for medical image interpretation when the imaging view is suboptimal for the target finding. The agent queried three independent vision-language models with progressively refined prompts, then used a verification step to audit reliability before committing to a forced-choice answer. The key insight is that when the imaging modality cannot definitively show the finding, the agent still must extract the best available directional evidence and justify the choice.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a finding is hard to assess on the given view, query multiple independent models with targeted prompts and aggregate their directional evidence rather than relying on a single assessment.\",\n    \"Use a verification/audit step to explicitly flag view limitations and conflicting model outputs before finalizing, then justify the answer based on the strongest available evidence.\",\n    \"Refine prompts across successive model calls to progressively narrow the question (from general description to specific laterality), improving the chance of extracting usable signal.\",\n    \"For forced-choice questions where the imaging view is suboptimal, commit to the option supported by the only positive directional evidence rather than abstaining.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical image interpretation\": \"Query multiple specialized models with view-aware prompts; explicitly note when the imaging projection limits assessment of the target finding.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus\": \"Use 2-3 independent models with varied prompt phrasing; treat agreement as stronger signal and flag conflicts for verification.\",\n    \"Forced-choice under uncertainty\": \"When no option is definitively supported, select the option with the most positive directional evidence and document the reasoning.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether the imaging view/projection can actually reveal the target finding before trusting any model's directional claim.\",\n    \"Check for agreement across models; if conflicting, run a verification step and justify the final choice with the strongest evidence.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":696,"total_tokens":1083,"completion_tokens":387,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":696},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":387}}}